/* model_geometry.comp -- the frame's alias model triangles
 *
 * One workgroup per alias instance (vk_instance.c): decodes the two poses
 * the instance blends (vk_model.c's compact model data), blends positions
 * and normals, applies the model-to-world transform, computes tangents,
 * and last frame's positions for the motion, and writes VboPrimitives and
 * their packed positions into this frame's instanced buffer
 * (VERTEX_BUFFER_INSTANCED), where the dynamic BLASes are built from.
 *
 * The vertex animation half of Quake II RTX's instance_geometry.comp
 * (src/refresh/vkpt/shader/instance_geometry.comp), with Hexen II's
 * compact poses and normals transformed by the inverse transpose (scale
 * types can scale x and y only, or z only). vk_model.c's check repeats
 * this on the CPU; keep the two the same.
